        "subject": "LU-21018 tests: ignore peers of foreign nodes in sanity-lnet",
        "message": "LU-21018 tests: ignore peers of foreign nodes in sanity-lnet\n\nOn a shared test subnet, a node of another session can connect to\nthe test node during a sanity-lnet test. LNet then adds a peer for\nthat node. Tests that compare the peer list then fail with\n\"Unexpected peer configuration\" or \"Unexpected config after import\".\n\ncompare_yaml_files() now deletes such peers from the expected and\nthe actual yaml before the compare. A foreign peer has\nan address on a local subnet, with a direct route. No node of the\ntest session has that address. Local, fake and router peers stay.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet\nTest-Parameters: nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I4bb65314d0e87a8457d802f4223eaa1210d688db\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
